        "answer_text": "Dominance: A dominant factor or allele expresses itself in the presence or absence of a recessive trait. For example, tall plant, round seed, violet flower, etc. are dominant characters in a pea plant. Recessive: A recessive trait is able to express itself only in the absence of a dominant trait. For example, dwarf plant, wrinkled seed, white flower, etc. are recessive traits in a pea plant.",
